# Paths excluded from the deployed static assets (gitignore syntax).
#
# Added 2026-07-28. Verified before this file existed:
#   https://murmuration.knowhere-group.com/.git/config   -> HTTP 200
#   https://murmuration.knowhere-group.com/.git/logs/HEAD -> HTTP 200
# The whole .git directory was being served publicly. No credential was present
# in the published config (remote is a clean HTTPS URL, checked), so this was
# hygiene rather than an active leak — but it should not have been reachable.
#
# Deliberately conservative: only build artefacts, VCS internals, and config are
# excluded. Documentation and every runtime asset are left exactly as they were,
# so this does not change what the site serves.

.git
.github
.wrangler
node_modules
_bc_backup

# Added 2026-09-17. Same gap as above, caught while deploying Cordyceps v3: none
# of these are git-tracked (.gitignore already keeps them out of source), but
# .assetsignore is the ONLY thing wrangler's asset uploader actually reads — it
# walks the real filesystem, so an untracked-but-present file still ships. Found
# live: .remember/'s local session logs (Windows file paths, no credentials),
# .netlify/'s stale site ID + local absolute path, and a stray simulation save.
.remember
.netlify
*-swarm.json

# Config and ignore files are not site content.
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore
.gitignore
.nojekyll
